<td></td></tr></tbody></table>The above table can help you prioritize where you still have most remaining upgrades to farm. In general when you have freshly reached level 85, your biggest priority will be to do <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=4926/blackrock-caverns">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Blackrock Caverns</span></a> every day. Not only does it have the most pre-raid bis items, the pre-raid bis items it do have are far ahead of the alternatives. <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56320/witching-hourglass">
<img alt="Witching Hourglass" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gizmo_khoriumpowercore.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Witching Hourglass</span></a> because it's just statted much better than other trinkets and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56297/armbands-of-change">
<img alt="Armbands of Change" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Armbands of Change</span></a> because there are no other 346 wrists. After that it will depend on what you are still missing. Grim Batol has one of the best trinkets to grab if you can't wait for Darkmoon Faire, <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=4945/halls-of-origination">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Halls of Origination</span></a> have several upgrades to make, <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5088/the-stonecore">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Stonecore</span></a> on the other hand has 2 items consdiered best but neither will be a big upgrade. <br/>
<br/>It is recommended that you first focus on heroic dungeon grinding, both targeting high priority dungeons and running 7 weekly randoms, before focusing on <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=794/archaeology">
<img alt="Archaeology" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Archaeology</span></a>. <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=794/archaeology">
<img alt="Archaeology" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Archaeology</span></a> can be done while waiting to get into dungeons. In terms of rep grinds, you will first want <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1158/guardians-of-hyjal">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Guardians of Hyjal</span></a> to revered, followed by <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1171/therazane">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Therazane</span></a> to exalted and last you can work on <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1172/dragonmaw-clan">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dragonmaw Clan</span></a> (H) or <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1174/wildhammer-clan">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Wildhammer Clan</span></a> (A) to exalted if you are not going to grab <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=67130/dorians-lost-necklace">
<img alt="Dorian's Lost Necklace" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_forestnecklace.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dorian's Lost Necklace</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56536/lightning-lash">
<img alt="Lightning Lash" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_leather_raiddruid_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightning Lash</span></a> or both.<br/>
<br/>Last you will do <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=794/archaeology">
<img alt="Archaeology" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Archaeology</span></a> grind, and here it is recommended to focus on tol'vir first as it has both ring and staff. If you get the ring, you can continue with tol'vir or move on to dwarf, choose the one you feel you solve fastest. The difference in DPS from staff is almost non-existant and shouldn't weigh heavier than what you can farm faster as it can take a very long time to get either staff.<ul class="last"></ul></div>